      "reading": "The evasion needs the operator's own queue to have drained before the challenge starts. Measured, an unbounded queue takes 39 to 61 milliseconds to drain at the lowest level and 1.38 to 1.46 seconds at the highest, against the half second it was given. Where the drain fits in the budget nothing is detected; where it overruns, the overrun executes inside the challenge window and is detected. So an operator that pauses on the challenge also has to bound how far it runs ahead of the device, which is an engineering requirement rather than a free win."
    },
